## Medium severity

### 2.1 `FLAG_SECURE` off in foreground — Open
- **Problem:** `shouldApplyFlagSecure()` in `MainActivity.kt` returns `false` unconditionally. The recents screenshot is
  blocked (Android 13+), but the foreground app can be screenshotted, recorded or mirrored.
- **Fix:** return `!isDebug`.
- **Regression risk (35–45%, UX):** users screenshot allowance and tax breakdowns to share with accountants and banks,
  and those would come out black. It also blocks bug-report screenshots and breaks screen-recording and UI-automation
  tools.
- **Decision needed:** enforce it in release, or make it a Settings privacy toggle.

### 2.2 Room destructive-migration fallback — ✅ Done
- **Problem:** both `PayslipDatabase.kt` builders used `.fallbackToDestructiveMigration(true)`, so any version Room
  could not migrate (including an unknown or future one) was silently wiped, and payslips exist only on the device.
- **Fix:** removed the fallback from both builders, in all build types. No shipped build ever had a schema below v5, so
  no legacy carve-out was needed. A missed migration is now a loud launch failure instead of silent data loss.
- **Tests (`PayslipDatabaseUpgradeTest`):** (1) a database with an unrecognised version fails with
  `IllegalStateException` and keeps its row (red before the change, green after); (2) every exported schema version
  upgrades to head, derived from `schemas/`, so the next bump extends it automatically; (3) a payslip row survives
  5→11. Tests 2 and 3 already passed (the migrations existed); they now guard the chain the strict policy depends on.
  Removing one `AutoMigration` makes both fail.
- **Verified:** full automated gate; Pixel 9 debug build upgraded in place over a populated database (Feb–Apr 2026
  payslips) with no crash or wipe; iOS simulator relaunch over its existing database.
- **Debt left:** no in-app recovery if a future migration is missed (launch crash until an update ships; a
  "restore from `.pcda` backup" path would be a separate feature). There is no native iOS migration test; iOS relies
  on the shared `AutoMigration`s. The stale `com.ssbmax…` schema directory remains.

### 2.3 iOS `x86_64` simulator link failure — ✅ Done
- **Problem:** `CLiteRTLM.xcframework` is arm64-only, so generic-simulator builds failed to link x86_64.
- **Fix:** `EXCLUDED_ARCHS[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = x86_64` in Debug and Release (2-line pbxproj diff).
- **Verified:** `xcodebuild` on generic iOS Simulator failed before and succeeded after.
- **Left alone on purpose:** Gradle `iosX64()` targets (removing them is a separate change). `iosX64Test` was not run.

### 2.4 Incomplete public `initKoin()` — ✅ Done
- **Problem:** registered only `sharedModule` (no `appModule`), so any caller would hit `NoBeanDefFoundException`.
  It had zero callers; iOS uses `ensureKoin()`.
- **Fix:** deleted rather than repaired, so there is one init path. Zero references remain.

